WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.548 --> 00:00:11.311
Mr. Ribbit, the science teacher, cleared his throat.

2
00:00:13.812 --> 00:00:18.453
"Ribbit! Do you know how we became frogs?"

3
00:00:18.933 --> 00:00:19.473
he croaked.

4
00:00:20.413 --> 00:00:21.954
The young frogs looked at each other.

5
00:00:27.575 --> 00:00:29.796
Mr. Ribbit held up two pictures.

6
00:00:30.588 --> 00:00:33.329
In one hand was a picture of a tadpole.

7
00:00:34.129 --> 00:00:36.370
In the other was a picture of a frog.

8
00:00:36.390 --> 00:00:40.971
"Today we are going to learn about metamorphosis.

9
00:00:41.591 --> 00:00:42.751
Ribbit!" he said.

10
00:00:42.771 --> 00:00:44.852
"Meta what?"

11
00:00:45.332 --> 00:00:45.932
asked Freddy.

12
00:00:45.952 --> 00:00:48.873
"Metamorphosis," Mr.

13
00:00:48.913 --> 00:00:49.673
Ribbit repeated.

14
00:00:49.693 --> 00:00:53.934
"It is how we change from tadpoles into frogs.

15
00:00:55.875 --> 00:01:00.216
In the spring male frogs attract female frogs by singing.

16
00:01:01.204 --> 00:01:04.207
The frog couple starts their family in the pond.

17
00:01:04.787 --> 00:01:09.030
Ribbit! The male frog fertilizes the eggs in the water.

18
00:01:09.751 --> 00:01:13.234
A few days later, the eggs begin to change."

19
00:01:13.254 --> 00:01:15.355
"Do they become tadpoles?"

20
00:01:15.936 --> 00:01:16.496
asked Hetty.

21
00:01:16.516 --> 00:01:18.658
"Ribbit! Yes.

22
00:01:19.479 --> 00:01:25.544
At this stage, the head is big and the tail is very long," explained Mr.

23
00:01:25.584 --> 00:01:31.426
Ribbit. "Soon the eggs hatch and the tadpoles come out.

24
00:01:32.126 --> 00:01:35.747
Tadpoles, like fish, use gills to breathe."

25
00:01:35.767 --> 00:01:37.208
"But Mr.

26
00:01:37.248 --> 00:01:39.749
Ribbit, we aren't fish, are we?"

27
00:01:40.269 --> 00:01:40.849
asked Lily.

28
00:01:44.591 --> 00:01:45.171
course not!

29
00:01:45.891 --> 00:01:47.792
We are amphibians.

30
00:01:48.612 --> 00:01:50.233
Who knows what that means?"

31
00:01:51.554 --> 00:01:55.935
"Amphibians can live on land and in water," answered Boris.

32
00:01:56.876 --> 00:02:02.502
"Right! But at first, tadpoles can only live in the water."

33
00:02:04.423 --> 00:02:05.944
"What do tadpoles eat?"

34
00:02:06.464 --> 00:02:07.064
asked Freddy.

35
00:02:07.084 --> 00:02:13.407
"Ribbit! As soon as they are born, tadpoles eat plants and algae.

36
00:02:14.187 --> 00:02:16.948
A few days later, they develop teeth.

37
00:02:17.849 --> 00:02:21.330
Then the tadpoles start to eat insects."

38
00:02:24.451 --> 00:02:28.601
Mr. Ribbit continued, "Tadpoles use their tails to swim.

39
00:02:29.341 --> 00:02:31.682
They are very active at this age.

40
00:02:32.423 --> 00:02:36.324
Tadpoles swim around in a group called a school.

41
00:02:38.665 --> 00:02:43.927
Six to nine weeks after they are born, metamorphosis begins.

42
00:02:44.387 --> 00:02:50.490
Ribbit! The back legs begin to appear and the tadpoles use them for swimming.

43
00:02:51.310 --> 00:02:55.432
The body grows larger, and the head begins to take shape.

44
00:02:56.228 --> 00:02:59.309
Next, the front legs begin to grow."

45
00:02:59.329 --> 00:03:02.291
"That looks like my brother!"

46
00:03:04.592 --> 00:03:05.352
Hetty laughed.

47
00:03:06.452 --> 00:03:11.995
"Ribbit! It looks just like a small frog except for the long tail.

48
00:03:12.875 --> 00:03:16.617
The tadpole is almost a frog now," said Mr.

49
00:03:16.677 --> 00:03:24.300
Ribbit. "During the last days of metamorphosis, the tail slowly disappears into the body.

50
00:03:25.020 --> 00:03:26.882
Remember the tadpoles' gills?

51
00:03:27.543 --> 00:03:30.225
Ribbit! They don't need them any more.

52
00:03:30.846 --> 00:03:33.508
The gills are covered over by skin.

53
00:03:34.289 --> 00:03:37.932
So the little frogs learn to breathe with their lungs.

54
00:03:40.355 --> 00:03:44.739
Once the tail is gone, the little ones can climb onto land.

55
00:03:45.379 --> 00:03:49.163
Now the tadpole is completely transformed into a frog.

56
00:03:54.440 --> 00:03:58.303
In a few days, the new frogs can leave the pond.

57
00:03:58.844 --> 00:04:03.247
They can enjoy life both in the pond and on land.

58
00:04:03.988 --> 00:04:07.671
Metamorphosis takes about 12 to 16 weeks.

59
00:04:09.012 --> 00:04:11.474
There are many different kinds of frogs.

60
00:04:12.214 --> 00:04:13.916
Some like to live in the water.

61
00:04:14.636 --> 00:04:17.158
Others spend all their time on the land.

62
00:04:17.779 --> 00:04:23.563
But we always have to return to the water to start our own families," concluded Mr.

63
00:04:23.624 --> 00:04:28.393
Ribbit. "Wow!

64
00:04:29.173 --> 00:04:31.594
We are special in many ways!"

65
00:04:32.275 --> 00:04:33.275
Victor exclaimed.

66
00:04:33.295 --> 00:04:38.338
"It's interesting to know how we got here," the young frogs croaked.

67
00:04:38.358 --> 00:04:41.259
"We are proud to be frogs!

68
00:04:41.759 --> 00:04:42.340
Ribbit!"
